// Two sources saw the same wrong output. The code is right only if both
// are wrong: 0.1 * 0.9 = 0.09, so it is wrong with belief 0.91. Each
// report can be wrong by 1 minus its bias, whatever their order.
evidence e { for f given x = 0 gives 2 trust 0.9 source "a" }
evidence e { for f given x = 0 gives 2 trust 0.1 source "b" }
